{"body":"## Summary\n\nDuring NF re-entry on Debian Trixie after confirming the host baseline was clean, `runtime_only` started successfully, but smoke/preflight entrypoints failed because installed shell scripts under `/opt/noemaforge` were not executable.\n\nThis does **not** appear to be a Trixie, GPU, Secure Boot, NVIDIA, or systemd runtime problem. It is an installed NoemaForge payload/packaging problem: scripts listed in the manifest and referenced by the dispatcher are installed under `/opt/noemaforge`, but they lack executable bits. One symptom is also misleading: the dispatcher reports the op smoke script as “missing” even though inspection shows it exists but is not executable.\n\n## Environment\n\n- Host: Debian GNU/Linux 13 (trixie)\n- Kernel: `6.12.95+deb13-amd64`\n- NoemaForge CLI: `0.33.0`\n- Repo branch during re-entry: `release/0.33.0-dev`\n- Repo HEAD: `71285d9 Document 0.33.0 pre-release candidate state`\n- NF start mode tested: `sudo noemaforge safe-start --wait --llm-profile=runtime_only`\n\n## What worked\n\n`runtime_only` safe-start succeeded and started only the safe core services:\n\n```text\nnoemaforge-llm-gateway.service active running\nnoemaforge-toolproxy.service   active running\nfailed units: 0\n```\n\nToolProxy also became active and exposed its socket:\n\n```text\nsocket: srw-rw---- 660 noemaforge:noemaforge socket /run/noemaforge/toolproxy.sock\nservice_active: active\n```\n\n## Failures observed\n\n### 1. Trixie preflight: permission denied\n\n```text\n/usr/local/bin/noemaforge: line 1219: /opt/noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-trixie-preflight.sh: Permission denied\n```\n\n### 2. MVP smoke: permission denied\n\n```text\n/usr/local/bin/noemaforge: line 1238: /opt/noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-mvp-smoke.sh: Permission denied\n```\n\n### 3. Smoke: misleading missing operation script error\n\n```text\n[noemaforge][ERROR] Missing operation script: /opt/noemaforge/tools/ops/noemaforge-op-smoke.sh\n```\n\nLater inspection showed the file exists, but lacks `+x`:\n\n```text\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 cat cat  6957 Jun 23 14:11 /opt/noemaforge/tools/ops/noemaforge-op-smoke.sh\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 cat cat 18676 Jun  8 13:24 /opt/noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-mvp-smoke.sh\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 cat cat 17892 Jun  8 13:24 /opt/noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-trixie-preflight.sh\n```\n\n`find` also confirmed related installed smoke/preflight files are non-executable:\n\n```text\n-rw-rw-r-- cat:cat /opt/noemaforge/tools/ops/noemaforge-op-nvidia-preflight.sh\n-rw-rw-r-- cat:cat /opt/noemaforge/tools/ops/noemaforge-op-smoke.sh\n-rw-rw-r-- cat:cat /opt/noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-firstboot-smoke.sh\n-rw-rw-r-- cat:cat /opt/noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-mvp-smoke.sh\n-rw-rw-r-- cat:cat /opt/noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-trixie-preflight.sh\n```\n\nDispatcher references expect these files to be executable:\n\n```text\n/usr/local/bin/noemaforge:741:  require_op noemaforge-op-smoke.sh\n/usr/local/bin/noemaforge:742:  exec \"$OP_DIR/noemaforge-op-smoke.sh\" \"$@\"\n/usr/local/bin/noemaforge:1219:  NOEMAFORGE_ROOT=\"$ROOT\" exec \"$ROOT/tools/prep/noemaforge-trixie-preflight.sh\" \"$@\"\n/usr/local/bin/noemaforge:1238:  exec \"$ROOT/tools/prep/noemaforge-mvp-smoke.sh\" --root \"$ROOT\" \"$@\"\n```\n\nManifest/checksum metadata also includes these scripts, so this looks like an install/copy mode issue rather than an absent source file:\n\n```text\nMANIFEST.json includes:\n- noemaforge/tools/ops/noemaforge-op-smoke.sh\n- noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-mvp-smoke.sh\n- noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-trixie-preflight.sh\n\nexecutable_manifest.txt includes:\n- noemaforge/tools/ops/noemaforge-op-smoke.sh\n- noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-mvp-smoke.sh\n- noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-trixie-preflight.sh\n```\n\n## Manual workaround verified\n\nAfter:\n\n```bash\nsudo chmod 0755 \\\n  /opt/noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-trixie-preflight.sh \\\n  /opt/noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-mvp-smoke.sh\n```\n\n`noemaforge trixie-preflight --json` passed:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"passed\": 9,\n  \"warned\": 0,\n  \"failed\": 0\n}\n```\n\n`noemaforge mvp-smoke --json` then executed and reached real application checks instead of failing at shell permission level:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"passed\": 36,\n  \"failed\": 3\n}\n```\n\nRemaining MVP failures were unrelated application-level checks:\n\n```text\npipeline_validate failed\npipeline_lifecycle failed\nselftest_core / testbench quick suite failed\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nThe installer/package step should preserve executable bits for all scripts that are invoked directly by the dispatcher or declared in `executable_manifest.txt`, including at least:\n\n```text\n/opt/noemaforge/tools/ops/noemaforge-op-smoke.sh\n/opt/noemaforge/tools/ops/noemaforge-op-nvidia-preflight.sh\n/opt/noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-firstboot-smoke.sh\n/opt/noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-mvp-smoke.sh\n/opt/noemaforge/tools/prep/noemaforge-trixie-preflight.sh\n```\n\nThe dispatcher should also distinguish between:\n\n- file missing;\n- file present but not executable;\n- file present but unreadable.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n1. Update install/package/copy logic to apply executable modes from `noemaforge/tools/prep/executable_manifest.txt`.\n2. Add a post-install verification step that fails the install if any executable manifest entry under `/opt/noemaforge` is not `-x`.\n3. Improve `require_op` diagnostics so a non-executable operation script reports `not executable` instead of `missing`.\n4. Add CI/release guard for the packaged `/opt` layout or release artifact mode bits, not only source-tree `bash -n` checks.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThis blocks operator diagnostics at exactly the wrong point: after `runtime_only` starts successfully, the next documented checks (`trixie-preflight`, `smoke`, `mvp-smoke`) fail before they can validate NF. It can mislead debugging toward Trixie, GPU, or systemd even though the safe core services are working.","comments":[],"labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOSdiUqc8AAAACjNlHzQ","name":"bug","description":"Something isn't working","color":"d73a4a"}],"number":212,"state":"OPEN","title":"0.33.0 install payload in /opt loses executable bits for operator/preflight smoke scripts","url":"https://github.com/Sinev-Maksim/NoemaForge/issues/212"}

